 2108: // /**
 2109: //    For a point (x1,y1) inside the element and a line segment (x1,y1)-(x2,y2), find the intersection point 
 2110: //    (xIntersect,yIntersect) and the side (intersectingSide) that it intersects.
 2111: 
 2112: //    Inputs:
 2113: //    @param x1, y1: point inside the element
 2114: //    @param x2, y2: other end of the line segment
 2115: 
 2116: //    Outputs:
 2117: //    @param intersectingSide:  side that intersects the line segment
 2118: //    @param nextElement: element that contains the intersection point
 2119: //    @param xIntersect, yIntersect: intersection point  
 2120: 
 2121: //    The equations for the two segments (the one we are considering and one of the sides of the element) are:
 2122: //    P1(tt1) = (x1,y1) + tt1*(x2-x1, y2-y1)  where 0 <= tt1 <= 1
